.TH DOWNJACK 1 "2026-11-12" "downjack" "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
downjack \- set up gitignore and license files like a lumberjack
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B downjack
.I command
.RI [ argument ]
.br
.B downjack gitignore
.RI [ name ]
.RB [ \-o ]
.RB [ \-d
.IR dir ]
.br
.B downjack license
.RI [ name ]
.RB [ \-f ]
.RB [ \-d
.IR dir ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B downjack
writes the boilerplate files a fresh project needs: a
.B .gitignore
for the language or framework you work with, and an open source license file
of your choice.
.PP
All templates are embedded in the binary, so
.B downjack
works offline and finishes in a blink.
.PP
Both subcommands take the template
.I name
as an optional argument.
If the name matches exactly one template, that template is used right away;
if the name is omitted, or is ambiguous, an interactive fuzzy finder is opened
to pick one (see
.BR "INTERACTIVE SELECTION" ).
.SH COMMANDS
.SS gitignore
Create a
.B .gitignore
in the project, or append a snippet to the existing one.
.PP
The selected template is appended to the file, prefixed with a
.B #-- \fIname\fP --#
comment that records where the snippet came from, and separated from the
previous content by a blank line.
Template names are those of the
.I github/gitignore
collection (for example
.BR Go ,
.BR Python ,
.BR Rust ,
.BR Node ).
.PP
Aliases:
.BR g ,
.BR git ,
.BR i ,
.BR ignore .
.TP
\fB\-o\fP, \fB\-\-overwrite\fP
Truncate
.B .gitignore
before writing, instead of appending to it.
.B downjack
asks for confirmation first.
.TP
\fB\-d\fP, \fB\-\-dir\fP=\fIdir\fP
Operate on the ignore file in
.I dir
instead of the current directory.
.SS license
Write a license file for the project.
.PP
License identifiers follow the
.I SPDX License List
without the
.B \-only
and
.B \-or\-later
suffixes (for example
.BR MIT ,
.BR Apache\-2.0 ,
.BR GPL\-3.0 ,
.BR MPL\-2.0 ).
Templates that carry placeholders are filled in with the current year and the
copyright holder taken from
.B "git config user.name" ;
if that name cannot be determined, the literal placeholder
.B <name>
is written instead, to be replaced by hand.
.PP
The file is written as
.B LICENSE
for plain text templates, and as
.B LICENSE.\fIext\fP
for other formats (for example
.BR LICENSE.md
for
.BR FSL\-1.1\-MIT ).
.PP
When the file already exists,
.B downjack
asks what to do: add a new file named
.BR LICENSE\-\fIID\fP[.\fIext\fP] ,
overwrite the existing file, or do nothing.
.PP
Alias:
.BR l .
.TP
\fB\-f\fP, \fB\-\-force\fP
Overwrite an existing license file without asking.
.TP
\fB\-d\fP, \fB\-\-dir\fP=\fIdir\fP
Operate on the license file in
.I dir
instead of the current directory.
.SS help
Print help for
.B downjack
or for one of its subcommands.
.SS completion
Generate a shell completion script. The script is printed to standard output,
so it has to be installed or sourced by your shell, for example:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
downjack completion zsh > "${fpath[1]}/_downjack"
.fi
.RE
.SH INTERACTIVE SELECTION
Whenever a template has to be picked,
.B downjack
shows a searchable list. Typing narrows the list down by fuzzy matching.
.TP
.B Enter
Select the highlighted template.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-P\fP, \fBUp\fP
Move one item up.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-N\fP, \fBDown\fP
Move one item down.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-V
Move one page down.
.TP
.B Alt\-V
Move one page up.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-C
Cancel; no file is written.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fP, \fB\-\-help\fP
Print help and exit.
.TP
\fB\-v\fP, \fB\-\-version\fP
Print version information and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including the case where the selection was cancelled or nothing was
selected.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred, for example the argument count was wrong or a file could
not be written.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./.gitignore
Ignore file written or extended by
.BR "downjack gitignore" .
.TP
.I ./LICENSE
License file written by
.BR "downjack license" .
.TP
.I ./LICENSE.\fIext\fP
License file written for a non\-plain\-text template, such as the Markdown
edition of
.BR FSL\-1.1\-MIT .
.TP
.I ./LICENSE-\fIID\fP[.\fIext\fP]
Alternative names offered when the target file already exists.
.SH EXAMPLES
Set up a
.B .gitignore
for a Go project, then let the finder choose from every template:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
downjack gitignore go
downjack g
.fi
.RE
.PP
Add an MIT license, or pick one interactively:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
downjack license mit
downjack l
.fi
.RE
.PP
Prepare the files of a project that lives in another directory, overwriting
whatever was there:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
downjack g rust \-o \-d ./my\-crate
downjack l apache\-2.0 \-f \-d ./my\-crate
.fi
.RE
.PP
Aliasing the tool to a shorter name is handy:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
alias dj=downjack
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR gitignore (5),
.BR man (1)
.PP
The bundled gitignore templates come from
.UR https://github.com/github/gitignore
.UE .
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at
.UR https://github.com/chardoncs/downjack/issues
.UE .
